# POLLY, songcopy: Copy song gives the target six patterns of its own, never one the source plays. Song 1
# plays P01..P06, its Main A P02 (a note recorded) and, as its Ending, P12 (a copy of P02): song 2's own P12 is
# the source's, so its Ending gets a free one (P06, no longer song 1's); P12 keeps its note. A flash error
# leaves the song unchanged.
wait 300
tap LFO
spin K1 2
wait 100
expect song_bars 1
tap HOME
tap PLAY
tap REC
tapkey 7
wait 600
tap REC
tap PLAY
wait 100
tap SAVE
wait 50
expect pat1_nev 1
# P02 copied to P12 (the pattern's jobs), and P12 made song 1's Ending
tap SEQ
press SAVE
wait 800
release SAVE
spin K1 1
spin K2 9
tap SEL
wait 50
expect pat11_nev 1
tap ENV
tap ENV
tap ENV
expect page 10
spin K3 6
wait 50
expect song1_style5 11
# Copy song 1 to song 2
press SAVE
wait 800
release SAVE
expect job 2
spin K1 1
tap SEL
wait 50
shot copied.png
expect song2_bars 1
expect song2_style0 6
expect song2_style1 7
expect song2_style4 10
expect song2_style5 5
expect pat11_nev 1
expect pat7_nev 1
expect pat5_nev 1
# a flash error while copying to song 3: the song stays as it was
flash_fail 1
press SAVE
wait 800
release SAVE
spin K1 1
spin K2 1
tap SEL
wait 50
shot flash_error.png
expect song3_bars 0
flash_fail 0
